From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:44:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(memory): recall skips notices, keeps the cache warm, cuts
 by section

Recalled memory (an external provider's <memory-context> block) is no longer recalled for a turn no person wrote: subagent results, relayed agent messages, process notices and restart notes (the user-message classifier of 0068, which now also knows background process heartbeats and the restart-continuation turn) get no prefetch, give providers an empty message at turn start, and queue no refresh, so a notice is never the next turn's query.

With memory.recall_history false the store keeps the recall a turn sent, and a later turn replays it byte for byte while the prompt cache is warm. Older blocks are dropped from the replay only at the last idle gap longer than memory.recall_cold_after_seconds (default 3600) before a user row, where the cache is cold anyway, and from the rows compaction keeps (except the newest user row). memory.recall_max_chars now cuts by section: the peer card, the session summary and the provider's answer stay whole (trimmed at paragraph or sentence ends only when they alone are too long), the newest observations fill the rest, the AI's self-description goes first, and a note names what was left out. The fence label says recall may be stale, from other chats or misattributed, and to prefer the conversation.
